24 cubes arranged in a rectangular prism in cubic centimeters with length, width, surface area? Answer: answer depends on arrangement.  

SA = area of top + bottom + left side + right + front + back.
if 1x1x24, SA = 24+24+24+24+1+1 = 98 sq cm, 
if 1x2x12, SA = 24+24+12+12+2+2 = 76 sq cm,
if 1x3x8, SA = 24+24+8+8+3+3 = 70 sq cm,
if 1x4x6, SA = 24+24+6+6+4+4 = 68 sq cm,
if 2x2x6, SA = 12+12+12+12+4+4 = 56 sq cm,
if 2x3x4, SA = 12+12+8+8+6+6 = 52 sq cm.

notice how the SA gets smaller as the arrangement becomes more compact.
